<title>USA: AutoZone, Frontier added to S&amp;P 500 index.</title>
<headline>AutoZone, Frontier added to S&amp;P 500 index.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>AutoZone Inc, Frontier Corp and Thermo Electron Corp will be added to the S&amp;P 500 index after the close of trading Tuesday, Standard &amp; Poor's said.</p>
<p>AutoZone, which is not currently in an S&amp;P index, gained 1 to 26-3/4 and was one of the most active stocks on the New York Stock Exchange.  </p>
<p>To make room for the new companies, Luby's Cafeterias Inc, Ryan's Family Steak Houses and Shoney's Inc will be moved from the S&amp;P 500 Index to the S&amp;P SmallCap 600 Index, S&amp;P said.</p>
<p>Frontier and Thermo Electronc will move up from the S&amp;P MidCap 400 index. They will be replaced in the MidCap index by NCR Corp, which is being spun off from AT&amp;T Corp, and UniSource Inc, which is being spun off by Alco Standard Corp, S&amp;P said.</p>
<p>The companies that will be removed from the SmallCap 600 list are Flagstar Cos Inc, L.A. Gear Inc and PureTec. These companies will not be added to another index, S&amp;P said.</p>
